    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (the other two test files are `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` support classes, not test classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`:\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Gets a logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- Reads the created `Owner` via `@Val` (the same mutated instance the pipeline threads through) and logs an info line with the owner id, `customerCode` and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, so it runs only after a successful save (when the JPA id, customer code and registration date are all populated) and before the 201 response. It carries `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with the surrounding steps.\n\nThe observed log line during the test run confirms it: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-10`. The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
